,"properties":{"cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.30.0","Node name for S&R":"MiniMaxH3ImageToVideo","ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.8","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":["H3-Context Assist-@zuanfilm\nhttps://chatgpt.com/g/g-6a72ee44de7481919daeee5879b328cc-zh3-gpt",1344,768,73],"color":"#422342","bgcolor":"rgba(24,24,27,.9)"},{"id":196,"type":"PrimitiveStringMultiline","pos":[-1806.1449899922886,4728.042305287833],"size":[590.984375,1292.984375],"flags":{},"order":12,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"value","name":"value","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"value"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"STRING","name":"STRING","type":"STRING","links":[514]}],"title":"H3 MINIMAX PROMPT","properties":{"cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.30.2","Node name for S&R":"PrimitiveStringMultiline"},"widgets_values":["subject_definitions:\n<Picture 1> is the first-frame reference for the target video, showing an armored female warrior centered in a chaotic medieval battlefield. She wears weathered red-and-metal armor and a battered metal helmet, holds a sword upright, and actively fights among numerous armored soldiers. Soldiers throughout the scene are simultaneously engaged in combat with swords and shields while smoke, fire, sparks, ash, and battlefield debris fill the background. The reference defines the opening character, active battle, environment, lighting, composition, and live-action cinematic realism.\n<Picture 2> is the last-frame reference for the target video, showing the same woman transformed into a regal crowned figure inside an aged stone ceremonial hall. She wears an ornate jeweled crown and elaborate deep-red gown with gold embroidery. Her face is close to the camera and visibly surprised and disturbed, as if suddenly experiencing a vivid vision. The image defines the exact final character, crown, costume, environment, expression, lighting, and composition.\n<Subject 1> is the same female protagonist across both references, maintaining recognizable facial identity and physical continuity while progressing from actively fighting warrior to crowned figure experiencing a vision.\n<Subject 2> is the ornate jeweled crown in <Picture 2>. Its polished metal and faceted gemstones provide the physical reflective surface through which the battlefield vision is revealed.\n\nsummary:\n[keyframe completion + reference generation] The target is a 7-second live-action cinematic sequence connecting <Picture 1> to <Picture 2> through one continuous unbroken backward tracking reveal. The opening begins in the middle of an active battle, with the female warrior fighting while numerous combatants fight around her. The camera physically retreats with large amplitude at fast, steady speed while maintaining her as the central visual anchor. As the camera retreats, the battlefield progressively becomes visible as a physically continuous reflection within the ornate crown, creating the impression that the crowned woman is seeing a vision of the battle. The reflection is optical and physically motivated, never a dissolve, morph, overlay, or separate image. The final frame reaches <Picture 2>, where the crowned woman is visibly surprised and frozen in the middle of the vision.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Picture 1> ([Shot 1] first frame): fully_preserved - The active battlefield, female warrior, armor, helmet, sword, fighting soldiers with blue armors , fire, smoke, sparks, ash, lighting, and opening composition are preserved exactly at the start.\n<Picture 2> ([Shot 1] final frame): fully_preserved - The crowned figure, surprised expression, jeweled crown, deep-red gown, ceremonial stone hall, lighting, facial identity, and final composition are reached at 00:07.000.\n<Subject 1> (throughout [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - The same woman remains the continuous protagonist. Her identity and facial structure remain recognizable while her appearance progresses from armored warrior to crowned figure.\n<Subject 2> (during [Shot 1] and final frame): fully_preserved - The crown becomes the critical reflective surface. The battlefield and fighting figures appear as a real optical reflection within its polished metal and gemstones, changing only through camera position, perspective, and visible reflective surfaces.\n\ndetailed_description:\n[Shot 1] Live-action cinematic medieval fantasy, beginning exactly from <Picture 1> at 00:00.000. The female warrior is centered in a close battlefield composition, wearing battered red-and-metal armor and a weathered metal helmet while gripping her sword. She is actively fighting: she blocks and strikes against nearby blue armored soldiers while numerous other warriors simultaneously fight throughout the background. Swords swing and collide, shields move through the frame, soldiers advance and retreat, fire burns behind them, smoke and ash drift through the air, and sparks erupt from weapon impacts. The battlefield is chaotic and continuously active, with multiple fights occurring around her. Her face remains the visual anchor despite the surrounding combat.\n\nThe camera immediately begins one continuous Pull Out / backward Tracking Shot with large amplitude at fast, steady speed, physically retreating directly backward while maintaining the female warrior as the central visual subject. The camera remains aimed toward her. No zoom, pan, cut, artificial reframing, dissolve, fade, morph, match cut, or image overlay.\n\nFrom 00:00.000 to 00:02.000, the camera retreats through the active battlefield while the woman continues fighting. Her sword performs defensive and offensive arcs, nearby soldiers attack and defend, weapons collide, shields shift, and combat continues on every side. The retreat reveals progressively more battlefield depth through natural parallax: fighting soldiers pass through foreground and background, firelight flickers through smoke, sparks cross the frame, and the environment expands naturally.\n\nFrom 00:02.000 to 00:04.300, the same uninterrupted backward movement continues. The ornate jeweled crown associated with the final state becomes physically revealed through the composition. The battlefield begins appearing as a real reflection across the crown's polished metal and faceted gemstones. The reflection contains recognizable fragments of the ongoing battle: the female warrior fighting, soldiers clashing, sword flashes, fire, smoke, and flying sparks. The reflection does not fade in and is not a separate image. It stretches, fragments, and shifts naturally across the curved reflective surfaces as the camera retreats and perspective changes. The woman remains the same physical subject throughout.\n\nFrom 00:04.300 to 00:06.000, the camera continues its uninterrupted Pull Out. The battlefield reflection becomes increasingly concentrated within the crown while the physical surroundings progressively resolve into the aged stone ceremonial hall of <Picture 2>. The woman's battered battlefield appearance continuously resolves into the elaborate deep-red gown and regal appearance of the final reference without morphing or dissolving. The crown settles naturally on her head while the reflected battle remains visible across its gemstones as though she is witnessing a supernatural vision.\n\nAt approximately 00:06.000, the crowned woman suddenly registers the vision. Her eyes widen, her eyebrows lift, her breathing catches, and her expression changes to unmistakable surprise and alarm. She looks directly toward the reflected vision while the battle continues moving within the crown's reflective surfaces.\n\nFrom 00:06.000 to 00:07.000, the camera completes the continuous backward reveal and reaches the exact composition of <Picture 2>. The crowned woman remains close to camera inside the ancient stone hall, wearing the ornate jeweled crown and elaborate deep-red gown with gold embroidery. She is visibly startled by what she has seen, eyes widened and face tense, as if receiving a sudden supernatural vision of the battlefield. The final visible reflection remains physically contained within the crown's polished metal and gemstones rather than floating separately in the scene. Her gaze stays fixed on the vision and she does not return to a calm expression before the final frame. The final frame must match <Picture 2> in character identity, crown, costume, environment, lighting, facial orientation, and overall composition.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nThe sequence begins with dense battlefield sound: multiple sword clashes, shield impacts, armor movement, running footsteps, shouted exertion, fire crackle, wind, and distant combat reverberating through smoke. As the camera retreats, the battle gradually becomes more spatially distant while the reflective vision produces a subtle ringing metallic resonance around the crown. In the final moment, battlefield sounds remain faintly audible beneath quieter stone-hall ambience and the woman's startled breathing.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA cinematic medieval orchestral score begins with aggressive low drums, pounding percussion, and rapidly moving low strings synchronized with the active battle. During the crown reflection, percussion gradually recedes while sustained strings and sparse metallic tones carry the transition, then hold a tense sustained note as the crowned woman realizes she is witnessing the battlefield as a vision.\n"]}],"links":[[393,161,0,160,1,"SEEDVR2_DIT"],[394,162,0,160,2,"SEEDVR2_VAE"],[395,165,0,161,0,"TORCH_COMPILE_ARGS"],[396,165,0,162,0,"TORCH_COMPILE_ARGS"],[400,169,0,168,0,"VIDEO"],[401,160,0,169,0,"IMAGE"],[412,178,0,186,1,"VAE"],[413,177,0,190,1,"VAE"],[416,179,1,190,7,"INT"],[417,115,0,190,5,"INT"],[418,115,1,190,6,"INT"],[419,180,0,179,0,"FLOAT"],[420,181,0,190,0,"CLIP"],[421,186,0,169,1,"AUDIO"],[422,190,0,183,0,"CONDITIONING"],[423,183,0,184,0,"*"],[424,177,0,185,1,"VAE"],[426,184,0,189,1,"CONDITIONING"],[427,184,0,189,2,"CONDITIONING"],[428,190,1,189,3,"LATENT"],[437,193,0,189,0,"MODEL"]